+/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ * Repaint registry
+ *
+ * Problem: the GDI blit into the NRB host is ONE-SHOT. Wine does not keep the
+ * content. On every redraw of the HWND (expose, restore after minimising,
+ * WM_PAINT, resize) the area is empty again; the user sees that as flicker.
+ *
+ * Solution: we hook into the WndProc of the target HWND (subclassing) and
+ * blit the most recently seen frame again on WM_PAINT/ WM_ERASEBKGND.
+ * In addition a maintenance thread periodically re-emits all dirty targets
+ * (fallback in case Wine replaces the WndProc).
